{"conversation":"Okay, I think the numbers that can appear in all positions after rotations must be in either the first top or the first bottom, since the final uniform value must be on every domino's top or bottom. So I will try to check if those numbers can be the uniform number, and count the rotations needed for each possibility.","python_code":"class Solution:
    def minDominoRotations(self, tops: List[int], bottoms: List[int]) -> int:
        candidates = [tops[0], bottoms[0]]  # possible uniform values
        min_rotations = float('inf')
        for x in candidates:
            rotations_top = 0
            rotations_bottom = 0
            for i in range(len(tops)):
                if tops[i] != x and bottoms[i] != x:
                    # impossible to have x in this domino
                    break
                elif tops[i] != x:
                    rotations_top += 1
                elif bottoms[i] != x:
                    rotations_bottom += 1
            else:
                min_rotations = min(min_rotations, rotations_top, rotations_bottom)
        return min_rotations if min_rotations != float('inf') else -1
"}

